.idea
/VIDEO
/video
/MUSIC
/AUDIO_PODCAST
/AUDIO
/audio
# Secrets. config.yml holds auth.secret_key, and `setup.sh --overwrite` writes
# .env.bak / config.yml.bak beside them — so the .bak forms must be covered or a
# later `git add -A` commits the JWT signing key.
# config.sample.yml does not match config.yml* and stays tracked.
.env*
!.env.sample
config.yml*
*.bak
# Nothing here generates TLS material, but offline mode requires HTTPS in front
# of :8000 and docs/OFFLINE.md walks through self-signed certs — which get
# generated wherever the reader happens to be standing.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.orig
*.rej
.claude/settings.local.json

__pycache__*
*.py[cod]
# Runtime data: cookies.txt, admin-recovery.txt, backgrounds, DB backups, and the
# default media roots. The contents are ignored but the directory skeleton is
# tracked — Docker creates a missing bind-mount source as root:root while the
# container runs as uid 1000, so every write under /data then fails.
# Note the `!/data/**/` line: git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory
# is still excluded, so the directories must be un-excluded before the .gitkeeps.
/data/**
!/data/**/
!/data/**/.gitkeep
.pytest_cache
.venv
node_modules
.ipynb_checkpoints
.next
.DS_Store
.ruff_cache
